{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00169",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.81,
      "end_seconds": 4.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Doctor? Hi. I hope I've got the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.25,
      "end_seconds": 9.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.21,
      "end_seconds": 23.77,
      "duration_seconds": 13.56,
      "text": "Doctor, it's breathlessness on the stairs. It's getting on my nerves now. I took the morning off to come in today. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.1,
      "end_seconds": 28.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.93,
      "end_seconds": 36.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "I'm not sure when it began, to be honest. Some weeks ago, but I can't say how many."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.29,
      "end_seconds": 48.75,
      "duration_seconds": 11.46,
      "text": "Go on. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.85,
      "end_seconds": 86.22,
      "duration_seconds": 33.37,
      "text": "It's every other day. Only resting, and it's not much. Climbing stairs definitely sets it off. I'd say severe. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. I've also had a racing heart sometimes, since yesterday. About racing heart sometimes, moderate, I'd say. And dizziness, too. With dizziness, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.78,
      "end_seconds": 90.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.37,
      "end_seconds": 103.76,
      "duration_seconds": 12.39,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.2,
      "end_seconds": 105.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "What about weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.5,
      "end_seconds": 110.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Um, not at all, no weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.43,
      "end_seconds": 114.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Any black stools, fainting, heavy periods or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.51,
      "end_seconds": 121.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "I mean, I haven't had black stools, fainting, heavy periods or chest pain, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.63,
      "end_seconds": 126.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.55,
      "end_seconds": 130.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.09,
      "end_seconds": 133.06,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.98,
      "end_seconds": 137.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "No, I don't smoke and never have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.97,
      "end_seconds": 140.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.29,
      "end_seconds": 152.26,
      "duration_seconds": 10.97,
      "text": "Yeah, it's omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day. I've never really been one for hospitals. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.37,
      "end_seconds": 155.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.09,
      "end_seconds": 156.96,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.98,
      "end_seconds": 175.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Right, have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.06,
      "end_seconds": 181.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Yes, uh, I had a lump removed from my back, years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.26,
      "end_seconds": 188.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.71,
      "end_seconds": 192.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "I'm allergic to shellfish, I get hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.24,
      "end_seconds": 197.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.07,
      "end_seconds": 211.66,
      "duration_seconds": 12.59,
      "text": "I, I have acid reflux. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.8,
      "end_seconds": 217.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known acid reflux. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.31,
      "end_seconds": 220.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.15,
      "end_seconds": 223.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.64,
      "end_seconds": 242.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, I don't hear any murmur."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.1,
      "end_seconds": 246.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.51,
      "end_seconds": 262.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Your eyelids are pale inside."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.98,
      "end_seconds": 271.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.66,
      "end_seconds": 275.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.6,
      "end_seconds": 285.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "Putting it all together, it fits best with anaemia of some kind. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.75,
      "end_seconds": 289.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.81,
      "end_seconds": 303.14,
      "duration_seconds": 13.33,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with anaemia of some kind do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had breathlessness on the stairs, severe, and no heavy periods or weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.72,
      "end_seconds": 305.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.46,
      "end_seconds": 330.58,
      "duration_seconds": 23.12,
      "text": "Let's get a vitamin B12 level, for possible deficiency. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'm going to order a ferritin level, for possible iron deficiency. I'm prescribing ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day, for three months. You take it by mouth. It's for possible iron deficiency. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.26,
      "end_seconds": 348.4,
      "duration_seconds": 17.14,
      "text": "Iron can darken the stools and bother the stomach, so take it after food. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.49,
      "end_seconds": 350.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.59,
      "end_seconds": 353.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Let's review you in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 354.75,
      "end_seconds": 356.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.64,
      "end_seconds": 364.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.18,
      "end_seconds": 376.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.09,
      "text": "So, uh, I take the ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.85,
      "end_seconds": 381.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.66,
      "end_seconds": 384.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "I appreciate your time, doctor."
    }
  ]
}